SPELLHELP

	cUsage:	n spellhelp <spell or psionic power name>
       spellhelp coverage

Displays school, classes and levels gained, domains and circles gained,
targets, augmentation rules, and documented effects. Damage entries show
amount and damage type; conditions describe their penalties and duration.
Labels appear in cyan and descriptions in normal text.

	cExamples:	n
  spellhelp deadly fear
  spellhelp magic missile
  spellhelp blindness

The help command also displays this output for matching spell or power names.
Full names and unambiguous prefixes work. Quotes are optional. Effects that
have not yet been documented are marked with a brief note. Use spellhelp
coverage to see overall documentation progress.

Damage formulas describe base mechanics; applicable global damage bonuses
and AC-cap modifiers are shown separately.
Feats, perks, class features, equipment,
and server settings may change the result. This command does not cast
anything or spend resources.
